CARRIED FORWARD
LESSONS (10 of 12 slots):
[L3] Lone *_latency_high: compare the metric to its own band. Two queries in ONE batch (literal UTC bounds, not now()): (1) deployments+config_changes last ~26h, all services, one UNION; (2) time_bucket(15m) pivot of p95/err/req/cpu/mem/dep over ~10h (metrics lag ~16min). Newest p95 in the day's band, or tracking req with flat err/cpu => dismiss (N1). 2 queries sufficed every time thru day 30 (p-039). (evidence: p-020, p-022, p-026, p-029, p-032, p-034, p-035, p-036, p-037, p-038, p-039)
[L6] Opening filter: deployments+config_changes for prior ~26h (all services, one UNION, literal UTC). Empty (p-026/30/33/36/37, p-039) or only other-service rows (p-027, p-034, p-038) => noise/vendor; dismiss fast. Other-service changes are decoys (p-002, p-008, p-015, p-025). Same-service change is innocent without an aligned step (p-023/24). Ignore changes stamped AFTER the page. (evidence: p-002, p-015, p-025, p-026, p-027, p-030, p-034, p-037, p-038, p-039)
[L7] checkout_error_rate_high: ONE pivot of checkout err/p95 + payment-orch pool_util/pool_wait/success/dep_latency/payments_db_cpu picks the mode. (a) pool~1, wait>4s, db_cpu FLAT ~0.30 => payments.max_connections cut (p-005, p-028). (b) pool~1, wait>4s AND db_cpu 0.30->0.85 => a payment-orchestrator deploy added a heavy query (p-031). (c) dep_latency/success broken, pool flat => vendor (p-011). 4/4. (evidence: p-005, p-011, p-028, p-031)
[L8] On checkout/payment error pages, first grep config_changes ~24h for payments.max_connections: cost-optimizer cut 100->20 at 09:00 UTC on days 5, 21, 22; pool exhausts ~19:00 UTC, page 19:05, oncall restores at 19:25 (remediation, not cause). If that key is ABSENT (p-031, day24), look instead for a payment-orchestrator deploy in the prior hour touching a query/DB component. 4x. (evidence: p-005, p-028, p-031)
[L9] Query shapes: now() is REAL wall-clock, not sim time - "now() - 26h" windows silently return ZERO rows (p-022). Always use literal UTC timestamps from the page header. Metrics go per-minute near now, so always time_bucket(INTERVAL '15 minutes', event_time)+avg(CASE WHEN signal=...) (raw pivots blow the 50-row cap). vendor_snapshots.published_at errors with "pytz"; omit or cast it. (evidence: p-005, p-009, p-011, p-022)
[L11] Timezones: handoffs and page headers quote PT, but event_time/visible_at in every table are UTC (PT+7). My MEMORY entries record UTC times. Before deciding a change is "hours before" or "right at" an alert, convert: e.g. p-005's config cut was 02:00 PT = 09:00 UTC and the page fired 12:05 PT = 19:05 UTC. Status: standard sanity check. (evidence: p-005, p-006)
[L12] The change list often includes remediation, not causes: oncall restoring a value an automated actor (cost-optimizer) changed, pod recycles/restarts, or a ROLLBACK deploy (rollback_of set, version goes backwards - day24 payment-orch v9.4.1 at 12:22 PT, 17 min after p-031 fired). Anything stamped after the page, or by oncall, is the fix; blame the earlier change. Status: standard filter. (evidence: p-005, p-031)
[L13] Vendor outages: the PayRail/Courierly status snapshot lands ~10-20 min AFTER our metrics break (p-011: onset 19:00 UTC, snapshot 19:17 flipping operational->investigating, "Elevated API errors in US West"), so query vendor_snapshots up to now, not just before the alert, and resolve with the snapshot event_id (vendor-<name>-<ts>). Status: worked. (evidence: p-011)
[L14] Decoys near a page: deploys touching only copy/UI/banner/help-link or another service, AND config changes touching only observability (day16 checkout.log_sample_rate 1->0.2; day24 checkout.log_level info->debug 2h before p-031, moved nothing). Judge by changed_components/commit_subject/key. Day 9/11/13/14 footers, 15 SKU, 22 banner, 28 help link (no page). 13 confirmations, none guilty. (evidence: p-005, p-011, p-013, p-015, p-017, p-018, p-019, p-020, p-021, p-028, p-031, p-037)
[L15] A deploy can bite ~25 min later: p-031 payment-orchestrator v9.4.2 18:35 UTC (changed_components=payment-enrichment-query) broke at 19:00. So don't reject a same-service deploy just because the step isn't instant; check changed_components for query/DB work and confirm with logs (QUERY_SLOW at payment-orch + CONNECTION_POOL_TIMEOUT at checkout). 4 queries total. Status: worked. (evidence: p-031)
KNOWN NOISE (1 of 3 slots):
[N1] *_latency_high on search, inventory, notification-worker, order-service is almost always false (30+). (a) evening ramp 16:30-21:00 UTC lifts p95, err/cpu/mem/dep flat, p95 tracks req (p-020/25/30, p-036/37); (b) p95 flat in its day band while req swings (p-022/24, p-026/29, p-032/35/38, p-039 inventory: p95 83-101ms all day, req 720->1419->922). No same-service change in 26h => dismiss. (evidence: p-020, p-022, p-026, p-029, p-030, p-032, p-035, p-036, p-037, p-038, p-039)

